      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "THE LAST TRIP (7) took charge early on and kept going to record a commanding 25 metres win last start over 1690m at Kilmore in his first run back from a break. Must overcome a very wide draw. Needs to be at his best to beat this field but he is up to the challenge. DON CRUNCH (2) went back last start then worked home in good style to finish 1.75 metres from the winner in third at Swan Hill over 2240m, that effort following a good second at Maryborough the run prior. Will enjoy a nice run from this favourable starting position. Needs to be at his best to beat this field but he has the ability to mix it with them. MEZZANOTTI (5) is worth some thought after finishing fifth first-up over 1690m at Maryborough last time out. COCOSWORLD (4) is the next elect off a last-start win by 1.3 metres at Maryborough over 1690m.",
